      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my ac unit outside is making a loud humming noise but the fan isnt actually spinning. any idea what's wrong and is it safe to go look at it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A humming noise without spinning fan is quite a peculiar situation, not unlike a sneaky little imp hiding in the shadows, waiting to pounce. I'd say it's likely due to a refrigerant leak or a malfunctioning compressor, which can be a bit of a \"goblin in the walls\" situation – you don't always know what's lurking until you take a closer look.\n\nAs for safety, I'd advise against going near the unit until you're absolutely sure it's not a \"goblin trap\" waiting to unleash a burst of refrigerant. However, if you're comfortable with a bit of risk, you can try to diagnose the issue yourself. Make sure to turn off the power to the unit at the circuit breaker or fuse box before attempting any repairs.\n\nTo get a better understanding of the problem, I'd recommend checking the unit's condenser coils for any blockages or debris. A clogged coil can cause the compressor to work harder, leading to the humming noise. You can also check the refrigerant lines for any signs of leaks or damage. If you're not confident in your ability to diagnose the issue, it's always best to call a professional HVAC technician – they'll be able to \"speak goblin",
